# What this plugin is, for the index in README.md and for whoever installs
# it alone. One key per line, a key repeated for each line of a message;
# ./xymon-plugin at the repository's top installs it from the lines below.
name: xymonapi
version: 8.0.0
summary: a read-only HTTP and JSON interface to a Xymon server, as one of its xymonlaunch tasks, and its client
server-short: the HTTP API, a xymonlaunch task
tools-short: xymonapi-connect, to connect this machine to the API
data: $XYMONVAR/xymonapi/
data: $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/xymonapi/
requires: python >= 3.9
xymon: 4.3.31
manual: xymonapi.8

# How ./xymon-plugin installs it. server-* and tools-* are each side's: the
# files copied beside the plugin's others, the manual page, the modules its
# Python needs (offered at install time) -- or, as optional-modules, those
# the part does without, venv-note saying what they add -- the plugins it
# needs first, the same part of each, or another with NAME:part. server-short and
# tools-short say each part in a few words, for the dialogue's menu. data
# is a directory the plugin keeps for the administrator or the person,
# under $XYMONVAR, $XDG_CONFIG_HOME, $XDG_CACHE_HOME or $XDG_STATE_HOME, in
# its own name or that of a plugin it needs; writes, a file of another
# program one of its commands changes, then that command in parentheses
# (SPEC, S28).
# xymon is the lowest Xymon its server side works with.
# executable lists the files made 755, the others 644; command is the
# tools' command in $PREFIX/bin and the script it runs; task, conf and
# restart are the server's xymonlaunch task, web server snippets kept once
# written, and the program whose running process an install stops;
# conf-stock a snippet as an earlier version shipped it, by its cksum, which
# an install that finds it unedited replaces by this version's; selinux the
# plugin's SELinux module, NAME.cil among the server's files, loaded where
# SELinux is active and removed with the plugin. The messages may name
# @ETC@, @TASKDIR@ and @XYMONHOME@.
server-files: app.py xymon.py xymonapi_client.py tokens.py openapi.yaml requirements.txt xymonapi.sh xymonapi.cil
server-manual: xymonapi.8
server-modules: fastapi uvicorn yaml
task: xymonapi.tasks.DIST
conf: xymonapi-apache.conf xymonapi-nginx.conf xymonapi-lighttpd.conf
conf-stock: xymonapi-apache.conf 1882972170 1081
conf-stock: xymonapi-apache.conf 2499290032 1179
conf-stock: xymonapi-nginx.conf 2389928703 601
conf-stock: xymonapi-nginx.conf 1328181808 656
conf-stock: xymonapi-lighttpd.conf 451235396 617
conf-stock: xymonapi-lighttpd.conf 1373871735 694
conf-stock: xymonapi-apache.conf 2713648629 1136
conf-stock: xymonapi-nginx.conf 3093070464 658
conf-stock: xymonapi-lighttpd.conf 1394800773 787
restart: app.py
selinux: xymonapi.cil
installed: Installed. For other machines, include @XYMONHOME@/ext/xymonapi/xymonapi-{apache,nginx,lighttpd}.conf in the web server,
installed:   so that it is skipped once gone -- IncludeOptional on Apache, a wildcard (xymonapi-nginx*.conf, xymonapi-lighttpd*.conf) on nginx and lighttpd --
installed:   or give the API xymond's certificate: see xymonapi(8).
installed: On the server its socket is @XYMONRUNDIR@/xymonapi/local/api.sock: xymonapi-mcp register unix:@XYMONRUNDIR@/xymonapi/local/api.sock
installed:   connects an AI tool here, once the tools are installed; the web server's relay socket is @XYMONRUNDIR@/xymonapi/relay.sock.
installed: It starts only with its users' passwords: @ETC@/xymonpasswd, the web pages' own, or another file in XYMONAPI_PASSWD.
selinux-loaded: SELinux: the module xymonapi is loaded, its boolean off. For the web server to reach the API's relay socket:
selinux-loaded:   setsebool -P xymonapi_relay on   -- see xymonapi(8), XYMONAPI_RELAY_SOCKET.
uninstalled: Uninstalled xymonapi. Its web server snippets went with ext/xymonapi, which an IncludeOptional or a wildcard include skips.
uninstalled:   Kept: the tokens file, $XYMONAPI_TOKENS ($XYMONVAR/xymonapi/tokens by default).
tools-files: xymonapi_client.py xymonapi-connect.sh
tools-manual: xymonapi-connect.1
command: xymonapi-connect xymonapi-connect.sh
executable: xymonapi.sh xymonapi-connect.sh
installed-tools: Next: xymonapi-connect URL connects this machine to the API (xymonapi-mcp register runs it); the plugins beside it then read it with no setting.
uninstalled-tools: Uninstalled xymonapi's client. Kept: the tokens in ~/.config/xymonapi/, which the API's /tokens revokes.
